---
source: crates/mrq-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[\"--help\"])"
---
A Markdown toolkit for the terminal: verify, lint, format, query, transform, render and display Markdown

Usage: mrq [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  toc          Print the heading outline of each file
  render       Render files or stdin to HTML, ANSI, PDF, Markdown, JSON or man
  validate     Check links, anchors, assets, footnotes, includes and frontmatter
  lint         Apply markdownlint-compatible style rules
  fmt          Format Markdown canonically
  query        Select parts of documents
  merge        Combine several files into one document
  interpolate  Expand `mrq:include` directives
  split        Split a file into one file per section
  stats        Count words, headings, links, code blocks, tasks and more
  diff         Structural, semantic diff of two documents
  show         Browse files in an interactive viewer
  lsp          Run the language server on stdio
  config       Inspect the configuration
  completions  Print a shell completion script to stdout
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
      --config <PATH>
          Use this config file instead of discovering `.mrq.yaml`

      --flavor <FLAVOR>
          Markdown flavor [default: frontmatter `mrq.flavor`, then config, then gfm]

          Possible values:
          - commonmark: Strict CommonMark
          - gfm:        GitHub Flavored Markdown
          - obsidian:   Obsidian: gfm + wikilinks, embeds, callouts, tags, math, comments
          - mkdocs:     MkDocs: gfm + admonitions, heading attributes, definition lists, math

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colors

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colors when writing to a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset
          - always: Always emit colors
          - never:  Never emit colors
          
          [default: auto]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Diagnostics output format [default: human, or github when GITHUB_ACTIONS=true]

          Possible values:
          - human:  Human-readable, with source snippets
          - json:   A single JSON array
          - ndjson: One JSON object per line
          - sarif:  SARIF 2.1.0
          - github: GitHub Actions workflow annotations

  -q, --quiet...
          Print less output; repeat for even less

  -v, --verbose...
          Print more output; repeat for even more
